    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nFirst of all, thank you so much for these plugins. They are great and straight to the point :)\r\n\r\nI was using mini.surround and trying to add `{}` around some lines using line-wise visual mode (<kbd>Shift+V</kbd>) but got unexpected results.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0 (homebrew bottle)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\r\n-- minimal.lua\r\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n  -- stylua: ignore\r\n  vim.fn.system({ \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\", \"--branch=stable\", lazypath })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(vim.env.LAZY or lazypath)\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\r\n\t\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.surround\",\r\n\tconfig = true,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn any file, visually select a couple of lines that have indentation (<kbd>Shift+V</kbd>) and try to add some surroundings like `sa{`. The text below is enough to see the issue\r\n\r\n```\r\nthis is a\r\nparagraph with\r\nno indentation\r\n\r\n\r\n\tthis is\r\n\ta paragraph\r\n\twith indentation\r\n\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI would expect the surrounding pairs to be added to either before and after the lines or at the beggining of the first line and end of the last one:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n this is a\r\nparagraph with\r\nno indentation \r\n}\r\n\r\n{ \t\r\n\tthis is\r\n\ta paragraph\r\n\twith indentation \r\n}\r\n\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe first one, with no indentation, works fine:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{ this is a\r\nparagraph with\r\nno indentation }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe second one is where we have some trouble:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tt{ his is\r\n\ta paragraph\r\n\twith indentation }\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I use visual selection (<kbd>v</kbd>) instead of line-wise selection (<kbd>Shift+V</kbd>), it kinda works, but the surroundings do not respect the line indents:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\tthis is\r\n\ta paragraph\r\n\twith indentation}\r\n```\r\n",
